    "lawCode": "Amd §4, Chap 668 of 1977",
    "lawSection": "Firefighters",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S2769\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to repeal section 4 of chapter 668 of the laws of 1977,\namending the volunteer firefighters' benefit law relating to\nprocedures applicable to a claim for benefits when a volunteer fireman\nsuffers death or disability due to disease or malfunction of the heart\nor of one or more coronary arteries, in relation to making the\nprovisions of such chapter permanent\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nThis bill makes permanent section 61 of the volunteer firefighters'\nbenefit law which requires that certain benefits for a volunteer\nfirefighter be paid unless shown by substantial evidence to the\ncontrary that the duties and activities of a volunteer firefighter did\nnot cause the heart disease or malfunction.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nIn 1977, the State Legislature found that volunteer firefighters often\nsuffered injuries or deaths resulting from heart attacks suffered in\nthe line of duty and that those claims of injuries from heart attacks\nwere often subjected to lengthy delays.  As a result, legislation was\npassed that established specific procedures to expedite the handling\nof these claims.\n\nWhat has become known to volunteer firefighters as the \"heart bill\"\nwas extended every two years from 1979 until 2005 when the Legislature\npassed a five year extension of these vitally important provisions.\nGiven the great history of this statute it would seem that now is the\ntime to make section 61 of the volunteer firefighters' benefit law\npermanent.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nA.9958/S.6986 of 2008\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
