    "lawCode": "Amd §4, Chap 668 of 1977",
    "lawSection": "Firefighters",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S2769A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act to amend chapter 668 of the laws of 1977, amending the volunteer\nfirefighters' benefit law, relating to disability due to disease or\nmalfunction of the heart or coronary arteries, in relation to extending\nthe expiration of such provisions\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nTo extend until June 30, 2015 section 61 of the Volunteer Firefighters'\nBenefit Law.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nSection 61 of the Volunteer Firefighters' Benefit Law requires that a\nclaim for benefits must be paid unless shown by substantial evidence to\nthe contrary that the duties and activities of the volunteer firefighter\ndid not cause the heart disease or malfunction.\n\nEvery two years since 1979, Section 4 of Chapter 668 of the Laws of 1977\nhas been amended to extend the expiration date for only two years. This\nsection due to expire on June 30, 2010, offers assistance to those\nvolunteers who are stricken while performing in the line of duty.\n\nOur volunteer firefighters provide an invaluable service to New York\nState and our individual communities. We, therefore, owe it to our\nvolunteer firefighters to extend this section of law to June 30, 2015.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n1999-00: S.742\n2001-02: S.2405/A.861\n2003-04: S.576/A.897\n2005-06: S.1401A/A.567A\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
